sequenceDiagram
    participant User as User Browser
    participant Route as OpenShift Route<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant OAuth as kube-rbac-proxy Sidecar<br/>8443/TCP HTTPS TLS
    participant Jupyter as JupyterLab<br/>8888/TCP HTTP
    participant CodeSrv as Code-Server<br/>80/TCP HTTP
    participant Elyra as Elyra (in workbench)
    participant DSPA as Data Science Pipelines API<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant S3 as S3-Compatible Storage<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant HF as HuggingFace Hub<br/>443/TCP HTTPS

    Note over User,Jupyter: Flow 1: User Accesses Jupyter Workbench
    User->>Route: GET /lab<br/>Auth: OpenShift OAuth
    Route->>OAuth: Forward request<br/>TLS
    OAuth->>OAuth: Validate OAuth token<br/>Verify workbench owner
    OAuth->>Jupyter: Proxy to backend<br/>HTTP (pod-local, no TLS)
    Jupyter-->>OAuth: JupyterLab UI response
    OAuth-->>Route: Response
    Route-->>User: HTML/JS application

    Note over User,CodeSrv: Flow 1b: User Accesses Code-Server Workbench
    User->>Route: GET /<br/>Auth: OpenShift OAuth
    Route->>OAuth: Forward request<br/>TLS
    OAuth->>CodeSrv: Proxy to nginx→httpd→code-server<br/>HTTP (pod-local)
    CodeSrv-->>User: VS Code UI

    Note over OAuth,Jupyter: Idle Culling Check
    OAuth->>Jupyter: GET /api/kernels/<br/>HTTP (pod-local)
    Jupyter-->>OAuth: Kernel status JSON
    Note right of CodeSrv: Code-Server fakes<br/>/api/kernels/ via<br/>nginx→httpd→CGI

    Note over Elyra,S3: Flow 2: Elyra Pipeline Execution
    Elyra->>DSPA: Submit pipeline<br/>HTTPS TLS 1.2+<br/>Auth: Bearer Token (DSPA secret)
    DSPA-->>Elyra: Pipeline run ID
    Note over DSPA,S3: Pipeline runtime containers execute
    DSPA->>S3: Store/retrieve artifacts<br/>HTTPS TLS 1.2+<br/>Auth: Access Key / IAM

    Note over Jupyter,HF: Flow 3: Model Download (pytorch+llmcompressor)
    Jupyter->>HF: Download model<br/>HTTPS TLS 1.2+<br/>Auth: API Token
    HF-->>Jupyter: Model weights
